  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={1,2,3}.$ Given that $R$ is symmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ | {{field-4}} |",
